    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The bias, RMSE and correlation can only be computed where both model and WOA23 data exist, so one common comparison mask must be built over all fields and applied consistently.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all three models and WOA23 on the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask over all of them with `build_comparison_mask` (WOA23 is part of this comparison, so `ocean_only=True` is right) and apply it with `.where(mask)` to every field before any bias, RMSE or correlation; scoring each model on its own pairwise cells makes the ranking meaningless.",
        "Report the shared-sample means the tools return (`mean_data`, `mean_reference` of `compute_difference_metrics`) together with the bias, and give the mask's cell count; the per-model native-grid means of Figure 2 are a different quantity from these shared-mask means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
