      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The requested delta_SST is a model-minus-observed-climatology bias, so the fragment's distinction between removing a model's own climatology and keeping the observed-climatology bias constrains what the mean bias means.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no anomaly, index, baseline or seasonal aggregation is asked for; only annual 1971-2000 climatologies are compared."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "`tos` is top-cell bulk potential temperature rather than a skin temperature, so its comparison with WOA23 0 m temperature carries that definitional caveat.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the top-cell bulk temperature including under sea ice (near freezing, not missing), so each global mean includes polar values near −1.8 °C; if a product masks sea ice, make the ocean masks consistent before comparing.",
        "`tos` is surface potential temperature, equal to surface in-situ temperature and different from Conservative Temperature; no `thetao` top-level substitute is needed because `tos` is supplied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Each model's global mean over its own native ocean grid must be area-weighted over the top level rather than a simple average of wet cells.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Every mean and map statistic is area-weighted over the top level: Σ tos·areacello / Σ areacello, with the weights masked to the same valid cells (`compute_basic_stat`, `op='area_weighted_mean'`); an unweighted `mean()` over latitude, over a curvilinear grid, or with land in the denominator is wrong, WOA23 included.",
        "Weight the difference statistics by area too: `compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default, and `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the pattern correlation—state that the quoted RMSE/correlation use area weighting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Native-grid global means should be computed natively, while regridding is only for the WOA23-grid maps and pattern comparison because it changes the land-sea mask.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute each model's global mean on its own grid with its own `areacello`; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the maps, the RMSE and the pattern correlation on the common mask, using 'conservative' (coarsening) and stating the method.",
        "An average belongs on the field's own grid because regridding replaces its cell areas with the target's, so native-grid and shared-mask means must not be expected to agree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20, so they must be CF-masked before any mean or sum or they will dominate the result.",
      "status": "summary_fallback",
      "fallback": "the notes failed the check",
      "violations": [
        "`um` is not in the selected fragments or the question"
      ],
      "rejected_notes": [
        "xarray decodes the CMIP6 fill 1e20 to NaN; code reading with `mask_and_scale=False` or `netCDF4` sees 1e20 at land, and a value near 1e20 (or 9.97e36) in any output is an unmasked fill value, not a result—use NaN-aware reductions.",
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables), and avoid a hand-rolled `(data*weights).sum('time')/weights.sum()`, which returns 0.0 on all-land columns instead of NaN."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are `gn`, which affects masks, conservation and which operations are exact on the native versus comparison grids.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its `tos` and areas are already remapped to 180×360 (conservative), so its \"native-grid\" mean is a mean on its 1° archive grid with a regridded land-sea mask.",
        "Resolution differs by ~2.5× between CESM2 (100 km) and MPI-ESM1-2-LR (250 km), so features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude—state this when describing the bias pattern."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245.md",
      "sha256": "be5515ae7b8c8826c4e329bddcd5cbadc8e3e000292b7f6e83e1537af36a990c",
      "reason": "The historical runs are coupled simulations with free internal variability and years not synchronised with observations, so the 1971-2000 model climatology versus WOA23 comparison must be stated as climatological rather than event-matched.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Coupled historical runs carry their own internal variability: a given model year is not expected to match the observed year, so compare statistics over the 1971-2000 window rather than individual years."
